      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely. High-GI foods that people with Type 2 diabetes should generally avoid include white bread, white rice, and most processed snacks. Instead, they can opt for low-GI alternatives like whole grain bread, brown rice, oatmeal, and fruits like berries and apples. Legumes, broth-based soups, and unsalted nuts are also excellent low-GI choices. Switching to these foods can help with better blood sugar control and overall health.",
      "source": "target",
